+Reading from a file
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+The module-level :func:`~rich.progress.open` function reads a file and displays progress as the bytes are read. The file is opened from a path, and the progress display runs for the duration of the ``with`` block. By default the file is read in text mode, and the total is the size of the file in bytes. Use ``"rb"`` as the mode to get bytes instead::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    with rich.progress.open("data.txt") as text_file:
+        contents = text_file.read()  # str
+
+    with rich.progress.open("data.bin", "rb") as binary_file:
+        data = binary_file.read()  # bytes
+
+If you already have a :class:`~rich.progress.Progress` instance, :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.open` returns a reader that advances a task as it is read. It does not start the display, and you pass the file path with an optional ``task_id``. If you omit ``total``, the file size is used::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    progress = rich.progress.Progress()
+    with progress:
+        with progress.open("data.txt", "rb") as binary_file:
+            data = binary_file.read()
+
+Reading from a file-like object
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+If you have an open binary file object, use the module-level :func:`~rich.progress.wrap_file` function. It requires ``total``, the size of the file in bytes, and it returns a binary reader. The reader does not close the file you passed in, so close it yourself::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    with open("data.bin", "rb") as source:
+        with rich.progress.wrap_file(source, total=1024) as binary_file:
+            data = binary_file.read()
+
+To use an existing task, call :meth:`~rich.progress.Progress.wrap_file` on a Progress instance. You can omit ``total`` if the task already has a total, and ``wrap_file`` raises a ``ValueError`` when neither is set::
+
+    import rich.progress
+
+    progress = rich.progress.Progress()
+    task_id = progress.add_task("Parsing", total=1024)
+    with progress:
+        with open("data.bin", "rb") as source:
+            binary_file = progress.wrap_file(source, task_id=task_id)
+            data = binary_file.read()
+
